plicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EGAMI MIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU MICHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CATALYSTS &amp; CHEMICALS INDUSTRIES CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EGAMI, MIKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, MICHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EGAMI MIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU MICHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EGAMI, MIKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coating fluid capable of forming a silica-based coating film having a relative permittivity as low as 3 or below and a low density and excellent in resistance to oxygen plasma and suitability for other processings; and a substrate having a coating film having such properties. The coating fluid is characterized by comprising a polymer composition comprising (i) an alkoxysilane represented by the following general formula (I) and/or a hydrolyzate of at least one halogenated silane represented by the following general formula (II) and (ii) a readily decomposable resin. In the formulas (I): XnSi(OR)4-n and (II) XnSiX'4-n X represents hydrogen, fluorine, C1-8 alkyl, fluoroalkyl, aryl or vinyl; R represents hydrogen, C1-8 alkyl, aryl, or vinyl; X' represents halogeno; and n is an integer of 0 to 3.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un fluide de revêtement susceptible de former une pellicule protectrice à base de silice, dotée d'une faible permittivité pouvant être inférieure ou égale à 3 et d'une faible densité. Ce fluide présente une excellente résistance au plasma d'oxygène et il est particulièrement adapté à d'autres traitements. L'invention se rapporte également à un substrat recouvert d'une pellicule protectrice dotée de telles caractéristiques. Le fluide de revêtement de cette invention se caractérise en ce qu'il contient une composition polymère comportant (i) un alcoxysilane représenté par la formule générale (I) et/ou un hydrolysat d'au moins un silane halogéné représenté par la formule générale (II), et (ii) une résine facilement décomposable. Dans les formules (I): XnSi(OR)4-n et (II): XnSiX'4-n, X représente hydrogène, fluor, alkyle C1-8, fluoroalkyle, aryle ou vinyle; R représente hydrogène, alkyle C1-8, aryle ou vinyle; X' représente halogéno; et n est un entier compris entre 0 et 3.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>